{"title":"Network Engineer Roadmap","role":"Network Engineer","summary":"A Network Engineer designs, implements, configures, secures, monitors, and troubleshoots computer networks that connect users, applications, servers, cloud environments, and devices.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Tech / B.E. (Bachelor of Technology / Engineering)","Course":"Computer Engineering"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career Overview"},{"type":"p","text":"A Network Engineer designs, implements, configures, secures, monitors, and troubleshoots computer networks that connect users, applications, servers, cloud environments, and devices."},{"type":"p","text":"For a Computer Engineering graduate, the strongest foundation combines:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Computer Networks","Operating Systems","Network Security","Routing & Switching","Cloud Networking","Automation"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Modern network engineering is increasingly moving beyond traditional physical networking toward SD-WAN, cloud networking, zero-trust security, network automation, observability, software-defined networking, and infrastructure-as-code."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career Development"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"Strong opportunities in enterprise networking, network operations, cloud infrastructure, cybersecurity and managed services"}],[{"text":"2030–2035"},{"text":"Greater adoption of cloud networking, SD-WAN, SASE, automation, zero-trust architecture and software-defined networks"}],[{"text":"2035–2040"},{"text":"Experienced engineers increasingly move toward network architecture, cloud infrastructure, network security and infrastructure automation"}],[{"text":"2040–2046"},{"text":"Potential progression to Network Architect, Cloud Network Architect, Infrastructure Architect, Principal Engineer or Infrastructure leadership"}]]},{"type