Systems + networking"}],[{"text":"Network Automation Engineer"},{"text":"Automated infrastructure"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"Employer Skill Matrix"},{"type":"table","header":["Employer Requirement","Importance"],"rows":[[{"text":"TCP/IP"},{"text":"Very High"}],[{"text":"Routing & Switching"},{"text":"Very High"}],[{"text":"Subnetting"},{"text":"Very High"}],[{"text":"Troubleshooting"},{"text":"Very High"}],[{"text":"Linux"},{"text":"Very High"}],[{"text":"VLANs"},{"text":"High"}],[{"text":"OSPF"},{"text":"High"}],[{"text":"DNS/DHCP"},{"text":"High"}],[{"text":"Network Security"},{"text":"High"}],[{"text":"Firewalls"},{"text":"High"}],[{"text":"Wireshark"},{"text":"High"}],[{"text":"Python"},{"text":"High"}],[{"text":"Cloud Networking"},{"text":"High"}],[{"text":"Monitoring"},{"text":"High"}],[{"text":"BGP"},{"text":"Medium–High"}],[{"text":"Automation"},{"text":"High"}],[{"text":"Communication"},{"text":"High"}],[{"text":"Documentation"},{"text":"High"}],[{"text":"SD-WAN/SASE"},{"text":"Increasing"}]]}]},{"heading":"Certifications & Learning","kind":"certifications","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Useful certifications can include:"},{"type":"h","text":"Networking"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Cisco CCNA"},{"text":"Cisco CCNP Enterprise"},{"text":"Juniper networking certifications"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Cloud"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"AWS networking/cloud certifications"},{"text":"Microsoft Azure networking certifications"},{"text":"Google Cloud networking certifications"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Security"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"CompTIA Security+"},{"text":"Cisco cybersecurity/security certifications"},{"text":"Vendor-specific firewall certifications"}]},{"type":"p","text":"For a student entering networking, CCNA-level knowledge is a particularly useful foundation, even if the student ultimately works in cloud networking or cybersecurity."},{"type":"p","text":"Certifications should supplement—not replace—hands-on labs and projects."}]},{"heading":"PG Options","kind":"pg_india","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Possible postgraduate pathways:"},{"type":"h","text":"Core Networking"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"M.Tech Computer Networks"},{"text":"M.Tech Computer Science"},{"text":"M.Tech Information Technology"},{"text":"M.Tech Communication Networks"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Cybersecurity"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"M.Tech Cyber Security"},{"text":"MSc Cybersecurity"},{"text":"Information Security programs"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Cloud & Infrastructure"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"M.Tech Cloud Computing"},{"text":"Advanced Computing programs"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Research"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"PhD in Computer Networks"},{"text":"PhD in Distributed Systems"},{"text":"PhD in Network Security"},{"text":"PhD in Wireless/Communication Networks"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A PG degree is generally not mandatory for entry-level network engineering, but can be valuable for advanced technical specialization, research or certain academic/government career paths."},{"type":"h","text":"Career Specializations"},{"type":"p","text":"After gaining experience, a Network Engineer can specialize in:"},{"type":"h","text":"Enterprise Networking"},{"type":"h","text":"Cloud Networking"},{"type":"h","text":"Network Security"},{"type":"h","text":"Data-Center Networking"},{"type":"h","text":"Network Automation"},{"type":"h","text":"SD-WAN"},{"type":"h","text":"SASE"},{"type":"h","text":"Wireless Networking"},{"type":"h","text":"Network Architecture"},{"type":"h","text":"Telecommunications Networking"},{"type":"h","text":"Industrial/OT Networking"},{"type":"h","text":"Network Observability"}]},{"heading":"Career Progression","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Technical Track"},{"type":"flow","items":["Network Intern","Junior Network Engineer","Network Engineer","Senior Network Engineer","Lead Network Engineer","Network Architect","Principal Network Architect"]},{"type":"h","text":"Cloud/Security Track"},{"type":"flow","items":["Network Engineer","Cloud Network Engineer","Senior Cloud Network Engineer","Cloud Network Architect","Infrastructure / Cloud Architect"]},{"type":"h","text":"Management Track"},{"type":"flow","items":["Network Engineer","Senior Network Engineer","Technical Lead","Network Engineering Manager","Infrastructure Manager","Director of Infrastructure"]},{"type":"h","text":"Emerging Technologies"},{"type":"p","text":"The student should monitor:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Cloud networking"},{"text":"SD-WAN"},{"text":"SASE"},{"text":"Zero Trust"},{"text":"Network automation"},{"text":"Intent-based networking"},{"text":"AI-assisted network operations"},{"text":"AIOps"},{"text":"Network digital twins"},{"text":"eBPF"},{"text":"Programmable networking"},{"text":"Network telemetry"},{"text":"Edge computing"},{"text":"5G/6G networking"},{"text":"Infrastructure as Code"},{"text":"Autonomous network operations"}]},{"type":"h","text":"AI + Networking"},{"type":"p","text":"AI can increasingly assist with:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Network Telemetry","Data Collection","Anomaly Detection","Root-Cause Analysis","Incident Prediction","Recommended Remediation","Human-Approved Automation"]},{"type":"p","text":"The engineer should therefore develop both networking expertise and data/automation skills."},{"type":"h","text":"Recommended Final Skill Stack"},{"type":"h","text":"Networking"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"TCP/IP"},{"text":"IPv4 / IPv6"},{"text":"Subnetting"},{"text":"Routing"},{"text":"Switching"},{"text":"VLAN"},{"text":"STP"},{"text":"OSPF"},{"text":"BGP"},{"text":"DNS"},{"text":"DHCP"},{"text":"VPN"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Security"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Firewalls"},{"text":"ACLs"},{"text":"IDS/IPS"},{"text":"Network Segmentation"},{"text":"Zero Trust"},{"text":"IPsec"},{"text":"TLS"},{"text":"Network Monitoring"},{"text":"Incident Response"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Systems"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Linux"},{"text":"Windows Server Fundamentals"},{"text":"Virtualization"},{"text":"Shell Scripting"},{"text":"System Administration"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Programming & Automation"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Python"},{"text":"REST APIs"},{"text":"JSON/YAML"},{"text":"Ansible"},{"text":"Git"},{"text":"Infrastructure as Code"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Cloud"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"AWS"},{"text":"Azure"},{"text":"GCP Fundamentals"},{"text":"VPC/VNet"},{"text":"Cloud Routing"},{"text":"Load Balancers"},{"text":"VPN"},{"text":"Private Connectivity"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Tools"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Cisco Packet Tracer"},{"text":"GNS3 / EVE-NG"},{"text":"Wireshark"},{"text":"Nmap"},{"text":"SSH"},{"text":"SNMP"},{"text":"Syslog"},{"text":"Network Monitoring Platforms"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Target Profile by Graduation"},{"type":"p","text":"A strong Computer Engineering graduate targeting Network Engineering should be able to:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Design basic-to-intermediate enterprise networks."},{"text":"Configure and troubleshoot routing and switching."},{"text":"Perform IPv4/IPv6 subnetting confidently."},{"text":"Understand TCP/IP at packet level."},{"text":"Configure VLANs and routing protocols."},{"text":"Analyze network traffic using Wireshark."},{"text":"Troubleshoot DNS, DHCP and connectivity problems."},{"text":"Work comfortably in Linux."},{"text":"Understand firewalls, VPNs and network segmentation."},{"text":"Implement basic network monitoring."},{"text":"Write Python scripts for network automation."},{"text":"Work with REST APIs and structured configuration data."},{"text":"Understand cloud VPC/VNet architecture."},{"text":"Build network laboratories using Packet Tracer, GNS3 or EVE-NG."},{"text":"Document network architecture and operational procedures."},{"text":"Understand basic incident-response workflows."},{"text":"Deploy and troubleshoot a cloud-connected network."},{"text":"Explain networking decisions during technical interviews."}]},{"type":"h","text":"Best Overall Positioning"},{"type":"p","text":"For Computer Engineering → Network Engineer, the strongest modern positioning is:"},{"type":"p","text":"“A network engineer with strong computer engineering fundamentals who combines enterprise networking, Linux, network security, cloud networking, automation and observability.”"},{"type":"p","text":"The career path should ideally evolve from:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Computer Engineering","Network Engineering","Cloud/Network Security","Network Automation","Network Architecture"]},{"type":"p","text":"rather than remaining limited to traditional device configuration and basic NOC operations."}]}]}